 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Lovely. A simple one to one swap is easiest. Each person keeps what they get, and donates the useless stuff to a charity that accepts it. Best test is a few drops on a white plate, and see if it fizzes. Okay, it' coming. The bell turns white when it' cold, so it' still cold. Sure, we finish about an hour. Front usually takes about an hour, and the back takes a bit longer because we skid in a second layer. Great. The front usually costs about eighty. About eighty dollars. They do it themselves in one hour and they' skid in a new layer, it'd cost them eighty times two, which is around twelve hundred dollars.",
